import AxQM.Core.FourGateReachableCircuitTower
import AxQM.Core.FourGateNamedRotationTower
import AxQM.Core.FourGateNamedReversibleTower

/-!
# The named four-gate tower submonoid, containing every reachable tower circuit
(N&C Exercise 4.43, named-gate assembly)

The universality argument of Exercise 4.43 shows the **operator density on the control tower**
(`exists_phase_smul_op_mem_closure_op_reachableTowerCircuitEvolutions`,
`AxQM/Postulates/API/FourGateReachableTowerDensity.lean`): up to a global phase every tower
evolution is a limit of the operators of the tower circuit submonoid
`reachableTowerCircuitEvolutions n θ` (`AxQM/Core/FourGateReachableCircuitTower.lean`), whose two
generating families are

* the single-tower-wire reachable single-qubit rotations `Evolution.qtowerSingleWire n i E`
  (`E ∈ reachableRotationGates θ`), and
* the `≤ 2`-control reversible tower gates `mcNotTowerGate n S t ht` (`|S| ≤ 2`).

The two per-family named re-expressions are `AxQM/Core/FourGateNamedRotationTower.lean`, which
shows the rotation generators lie in the submonoid generated by the single-wire placements of
`{hadamardGate, sGate, rotZGate θ}` (`qtowerSingleWire_mem_namedRotationTowerGates`), and
`AxQM/Core/FourGateNamedReversibleTower.lean`, which identifies the reversible gates' `Cᵏ(X)` cores
with the named gates `cnotGate` / `toffoliGate` for `|S| ≤ 2`
(`placedMcCtrlX_{one,two}_eq_onWires_{…}`).

**This file assembles both halves into one submonoid generated by the four named gates and shows the
whole reachable tower submonoid lies inside it.** Density then transfers to the named submonoid by a
single `closure_mono` step (`AxQM/Postulates/API/FourGateNamedTowerDensity.lean`).

## What is formalised

* `namedMcNotGate k` — the **named `≤ 2`-control reversible gate**: `NOT = H·S²·H` (`k = 0`),
  `cnotGate` (`k = 1`), `toffoliGate` (`k = 2`), and the raw `mcCtrl (k) pauliXGate` filler for the
  unused `k ≥ 3`. The `k = 0` value is the `{H, S}` circuit `H·S²·H` (not a bare `pauliXGate`), so
  the generating set below names *exactly* the four gates `H, S, CNOT, Toffoli` — no separate fifth
  gate `X`. Keeping the arity `k` symbolic (rather than case-splitting `S.card` at the placed
  gate, whose wire count and permutation depend on `S.card`) is what makes the membership proof go
  through by a single core rewrite.
* `mcCtrl_pauliXGate_eq_namedMcNotGate` — **the core identification**: `mcCtrl k pauliXGate =
  namedMcNotGate k` for `k ≤ 2`, from the reversible-core lemmas `mcCtrl_zero` +
  `pauliXGate_eq_hadamardGate_sGateSq` (`k = 0`), `mcCtrl_one_pauliXGate_eq_cnotGate` (`k = 1`) and
  `mcCtrl_two_pauliXGate_eq_toffoliGate` (`k = 2`).
* `namedFourGateTowerGates n θ` — **the named four-gate tower submonoid**: the submonoid of
  `Evolution (qtower n qubit)` generated by
  - the single-tower-wire placements `Evolution.qtowerSingleWire n i g` of the three named gates
    `g ∈ {hadamardGate, sGate, rotZGate θ}` (over every wire `i`), and
  - the named reversible gates `namedMcNotGate k` (`k ≤ 2`) placed on an arbitrary wire set and
    transported onto the tower — the exact form `placedMcNot` produces, with its raw `Cᵏ(X)` core
    replaced by the named gate.

  Its generators are only the four gates `hadamardGate, sGate, cnotGate, toffoliGate` (through
  `namedMcNotGate`) together with the measurement-realised base rotation `rotZGate θ` (Exercise
  4.41, the gate the four *unitary* gates alone cannot supply).
* `namedRotationTowerGates_le_namedFourGateTowerGates` — the named rotation tower submonoid is a
  sub-submonoid (its generators are the left half of the generating set; `Submonoid.closure_mono`).
* `mcNotTowerGate_mem_namedFourGateTowerGates` — **the reversible membership**: for `|S| ≤ 2` the
  reversible tower gate `mcNotTowerGate n S t ht` lies in `namedFourGateTowerGates n θ`.
  Unfolding `mcNotTowerGate` / `Evolution.placedMcNot` / `Evolution.placedMcCtrlX` /
  `Evolution.tensorPowMcCtrlX` exposes the raw core `mcCtrl (S.card) pauliXGate`, which the core
  identification `mcCtrl_pauliXGate_eq_namedMcNotGate` rewrites to `namedMcNotGate (S.card)` —
  turning the gate into exactly a named reversible generator (the wire count and permutation are
  read off by unification).
* `reachableTowerCircuitEvolutions_le_namedFourGateTowerGates` — **the containment**: the whole
  grounded reachable tower submonoid is contained in the named four-gate tower submonoid,

    `reachableTowerCircuitEvolutions n θ ≤ namedFourGateTowerGates n θ`,

  by `Submonoid.closure_le`: the rotation generators land via
  `qtowerSingleWire_mem_namedRotationTowerGates` + the sub-submonoid inclusion, the reversible
  generators via `mcNotTowerGate_mem_namedFourGateTowerGates`. Every reachable tower circuit is
  thus a circuit of the four *named* gates (with measurement) on tower wires, so density transfers.
-/

namespace AxQM

noncomputable section

/-- **The named `≤ 2`-control reversible gate.** The multiply-controlled `NOT` with `k` controls,
for the reachable range `k ≤ 2`, as one of the named gates: `NOT = H·S²·H` (`k = 0`), the named CNOT
`cnotGate` (`k = 1`), the named Toffoli `toffoliGate` (`k = 2`); for the unused `k ≥ 3` it is the
raw `mcCtrl k pauliXGate` (a filler, never referenced by the reachable generators). The `k = 0`
value is the `{H, S}` circuit `H·S²·H` (`= pauliXGate` by `pauliXGate_eq_hadamardGate_sGateSq`), so
`namedFourGateTowerGates` is generated by *exactly* the four gates `H, S, CNOT, Toffoli` — the `NOT`
is not a separate fifth gate but the `{H, S}` realisation. Its type
`Evolution (qtower k qubit)` matches the core of `Evolution.tensorPowMcCtrlX k`
(`mcCtrl k pauliXGate`), via
`mcCtrl_pauliXGate_eq_namedMcNotGate`. -/
def namedMcNotGate : (k : ℕ) → Evolution (qtower k qubit)
  | 0 => hadamardGate.comp ((sGate.comp sGate).comp hadamardGate)
  | 1 => cnotGate
  | 2 => toffoliGate
  | (k + 3) => mcCtrl (k + 3) pauliXGate

/-- **The multiply-controlled `NOT` core is the named reversible gate.** For the reachable range
`k ≤ 2`, the `Cᵏ(X)` core `mcCtrl k pauliXGate` is the named gate `namedMcNotGate k`:

  `mcCtrl k pauliXGate = namedMcNotGate k`.

The three cases are the reversible-core identifications: `k = 0` is
`mcCtrl 0 pauliXGate = pauliXGate = H·S²·H` (`mcCtrl_zero` + `pauliXGate_eq_hadamardGate_sGateSq`);
`k = 1` is
`mcCtrl_one_pauliXGate_eq_cnotGate`; `k = 2` is `mcCtrl_two_pauliXGate_eq_toffoliGate`. This is the
one rewrite the reversible membership performs, so keeping `k` symbolic here (rather than at the
placed gate) confines the case split to this non-dependent core equality. -/
theorem mcCtrl_pauliXGate_eq_namedMcNotGate (k : ℕ) (hk : k ≤ 2) :
    mcCtrl k pauliXGate = namedMcNotGate k := by
  interval_cases k
  · rw [mcCtrl_zero]; exact pauliXGate_eq_hadamardGate_sGateSq
  · exact mcCtrl_one_pauliXGate_eq_cnotGate
  · exact mcCtrl_two_pauliXGate_eq_toffoliGate

/-- **The named `≤ 2`-control reversible tower generators.** The right-hand generator family of both
`namedFourGateTowerGates` and its measurement-realised refinement `fourGateMeasurementReachable`
(`Postulates/API/FourGateMeasurementUniversal`): the named reversible gates `namedMcNotGate k`
(`k ≤ 2` — a `NOT`/`CNOT`/`Toffoli`) placed on an arbitrary wire set by `Evolution.onWires` and
transported onto the tower — the exact form `Evolution.placedMcNot` produces (`Evolution.congr
(qtowerQubitTensorPow n).symm` of a `QSystem.tensorPowCongr`-cast `onWires` gate), with its raw
`mcCtrl k pauliXGate` core replaced by the named gate. It is a shared definition so the two
submonoids differ *only* in their rotation-generator half. -/
def namedReversibleTowerGenerators (n : ℕ) : Set (Evolution (qtower n qubit)) :=
  {E | ∃ (k b : ℕ) (_ : k ≤ 2) (σ : Equiv.Perm (Fin (k + 1 + b))) (h : k + 1 + b = n + 1),
      E = Evolution.congr (qtowerQubitTensorPow n).symm
            (((Evolution.congr (qtowerQubitTensorPow k) (namedMcNotGate k)).onWires b σ).congr
              (QSystem.tensorPowCongr qubit (finCongr h)))}

/-- **The named four-gate tower submonoid.** The submonoid of `Evolution (qtower n qubit)` generated
by the two named generator families:

* the single-tower-wire placements `Evolution.qtowerSingleWire n i g` of the three named gates
  `g ∈ {hadamardGate, sGate, rotZGate θ}`, over every wire `i` (the rotation half), and
* the named reversible gates `namedMcNotGate k` (`k ≤ 2` — a `NOT`/`CNOT`/`Toffoli`) placed on an
  arbitrary wire set by `Evolution.onWires` and transported onto the tower — the exact form
  `Evolution.placedMcNot` produces (`Evolution.congr (qtowerQubitTensorPow n).symm` of a
  `QSystem.tensorPowCongr`-cast `onWires` gate), with its raw `mcCtrl k pauliXGate` core replaced by
  the named gate.

Every generator is one of the four gates `hadamardGate, sGate, cnotGate, toffoliGate` (through
`namedMcNotGate`) or the base rotation `rotZGate θ` (realised separately by the Exercise 4.41
measurement circuit). It contains the whole reachable tower submonoid
(`reachableTowerCircuitEvolutions_le_namedFourGateTowerGates`). -/
noncomputable def namedFourGateTowerGates (n : ℕ) (θ : ℝ) :
    Submonoid (Evolution (qtower n qubit)) :=
  Submonoid.closure
    ((⋃ i : Fin (n + 1),
        Evolution.qtowerSingleWire n i ''
          ({hadamardGate, sGate, rotZGate θ} : Set (Evolution qubit))) ∪
      namedReversibleTowerGenerators n)

/-- **The named rotation tower submonoid sits inside the named four-gate tower submonoid.** The
generators of `namedRotationTowerGates n θ` (the single-wire placements of `hadamardGate, sGate,
rotZGate θ`) are the left half of the generating set of `namedFourGateTowerGates n θ`, so
`Submonoid.closure_mono` gives `namedRotationTowerGates n θ ≤ namedFourGateTowerGates n θ`. -/
theorem namedRotationTowerGates_le_namedFourGateTowerGates (n : ℕ) (θ : ℝ) :
    namedRotationTowerGates n θ ≤ namedFourGateTowerGates n θ :=
  Submonoid.closure_mono Set.subset_union_left

/-- **The grounded reversible tower gate is a named four-gate tower gate.** For `|S| ≤ 2` the
grounded reversible tower gate `mcNotTowerGate n S t ht` lies in `namedFourGateTowerGates n θ`.

`mcNotTowerGate n S t ht` unfolds to `Evolution.congr (qtowerQubitTensorPow n).symm` of the
register-cast placed block `Evolution.placedMcCtrlX (S.card) b σ`, and `placedMcCtrlX` /
`tensorPowMcCtrlX` expose its raw core `mcCtrl (S.card) pauliXGate`; the core identification
`mcCtrl_pauliXGate_eq_namedMcNotGate (S.card) hcard` rewrites it to `namedMcNotGate (S.card)`. The
result is exactly a named reversible generator (`k := S.card`; the wire count `b` and permutation
`σ` of `placedMcNot`, and the register-cast proof `card_succ_add_sub`, are read off by unification),
so
`Submonoid.subset_closure` closes the membership. -/
theorem mcNotTowerGate_mem_namedFourGateTowerGates {n : ℕ} {θ : ℝ} (S : Finset (Fin (n + 1)))
    (t : Fin (n + 1)) (ht : t ∉ S) (hcard : S.card ≤ 2) :
    mcNotTowerGate n S t ht ∈ namedFourGateTowerGates n θ := by
  apply Submonoid.subset_closure
  apply Or.inr
  rw [mcNotTowerGate, Evolution.placedMcNot, Evolution.placedMcCtrlX_def,
    Evolution.tensorPowMcCtrlX_def, mcCtrl_pauliXGate_eq_namedMcNotGate S.card hcard]
  exact ⟨S.card, _, hcard, _, _, rfl⟩

/-- **Every grounded reachable tower circuit is a named four-gate tower circuit.** The whole
grounded reachable tower circuit submonoid is contained in the named four-gate tower submonoid:

  `reachableTowerCircuitEvolutions n θ ≤ namedFourGateTowerGates n θ`.

By `Submonoid.closure_le` it suffices to place each of the two generator families of
`reachableTowerCircuitEvolutions n θ` inside `namedFourGateTowerGates n θ`: a single-tower-wire
reachable rotation gate `Evolution.qtowerSingleWire n i E` (`E ∈ reachableRotationGates θ`) via
`qtowerSingleWire_mem_namedRotationTowerGates` and the sub-submonoid inclusion
`namedRotationTowerGates_le_namedFourGateTowerGates`; a `≤ 2`-control grounded reversible gate
`mcNotTowerGate n S t ht` via `mcNotTowerGate_mem_namedFourGateTowerGates`.

This step re-expresses every generator of the grounded tower
submonoid over the four *named* gates `hadamardGate, sGate, cnotGate, toffoliGate` (with the
measurement-realised `rotZGate θ`), so the tower operator density
(`exists_phase_smul_op_mem_closure_op_reachableTowerCircuitEvolutions`) transfers to the named
submonoid by `closure_mono`. -/
theorem reachableTowerCircuitEvolutions_le_namedFourGateTowerGates (n : ℕ) (θ : ℝ) :
    reachableTowerCircuitEvolutions n θ ≤ namedFourGateTowerGates n θ := by
  rw [reachableTowerCircuitEvolutions]
  refine Submonoid.closure_le.2 ?_
  rintro x (hrot | hrev)
  · rw [Set.mem_iUnion] at hrot
    obtain ⟨i, E, hE, rfl⟩ := hrot
    exact namedRotationTowerGates_le_namedFourGateTowerGates n θ
      (qtowerSingleWire_mem_namedRotationTowerGates i hE)
  · obtain ⟨S, t, ht, hcard, rfl⟩ := hrev
    exact mcNotTowerGate_mem_namedFourGateTowerGates S t ht hcard

end

end AxQM
